10	 * Measured against the committed capture (`fixtures/cc-2.1.234/`, 2 sessions,
11	 * 5 sidecars, 22 `tool_use` blocks of which 4 are named `Agent`):
12	 *
13	 *   toolu_017Pp1K6YSjX4SBuJDcmMsKs  main 05c5482d…  -> agent a69e0f453d5ca5f43  depth 1
14	 *   toolu_01MiUaF4vR8zVMp5nL8njJH6  main 05c5482d…  -> agent a32b33ebf1b92e214  depth 1
15	 *   toolu_015U2QmdfzyqUd6DrCmCxfFB  main 05c5482d…  -> agent a1a53f42c5eca8824  depth 1
16	 *   toolu_012xCBtQH1ejFcfwn9E1pkAw  agent a1a53f42… -> agent a3ecf86bbfb853726  depth 2
17	 *   toolu_018fbDjBX1ah7FTXs727doeC  main 4299490e…  -> agent a5e718f3cb731b607  depth 1
18	 *
19	 * Every id occurs exactly once as a `tool_use` id across the whole capture, so
20	 * all 5 resolve, 0 are ambiguous and 0 are unresolved. The depth-2 agent's
21	 * parent is another *agent* transcript, not the main one.
22	 *
23	 * Grounding constraints this module is held to:
24	 *
25	 *   G1  Read-only. {@link attributeSubagents} does no I/O at all;
26	 *       {@link loadSessionForAttribution} opens transcripts with `readFile`
27	 *       and writes nothing, anywhere.
28	 *   G3  Refuse, don't guess. This is the whole module. A key that matches
29	 *       nothing yields `unresolved`; a key that matches twice yields
30	 *       `ambiguous`. There is deliberately no nearest-match, no timestamp
31	 *       proximity, no "last remaining candidate", and no fallback to the main
32	 *       transcript. A wrong parent looks exactly like a right one once the
33	 *       tree is drawn, so a guess here is unrecoverable corruption.
